  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Conveyor Project Risk Management Facility Technical Assistance (Buy-in GCIEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To design a fit-for-purpose Risk Management Facility (RMF) for the Jordanian Aqaba Amman Water Desalination and Conveyance Project (AAWDCP), or National Conveyor Project (NCP) construction phase. The design phase will allow us to establish a clear governance and stakeholder coordination framework to facilitate efficient decision making and clear risk identification early on, whilst also mobilising a multi-disciplinary team and identifying the core RMF tooling requirements. The design process will result in a detailed Terms of Reference (TOR) for the RMF Inception Phase of the Jordan buy-in (November 2025 to March 2026), including institutional roles, key deliverables, team structure, risk prioritisation tools, and coordination frameworks. The approach will ensure that Green Cities Infrastructure and Environment Programme (GCIEP)&#x2019;s risk governance methods are adapted to Jordan&#x2019;s context and that design-to-delivery continuity is preserved.</narrative>
  </description>
